## Module 2: System Stakeholders, Personas & User Journeys

### 2.1 Persona Definitions

1. **The Casual Seller (Individual Upgrader):**
* *Goal:* Offload an older flagship device (e.g., iPhone 13 Pro) quickly without endless price hagglers.
* *Requirement:* Guided listing workflow, auto-calculated appraisal, guaranteed data privacy protections.


2. **The Budget-Conscious Buyer:**
* *Goal:* Purchase an authenticated, high-performance device at 40–60% below retail MSRP.
* *Requirement:* Verified battery health reports, cosmetic condition grading transparency, warranty assurance.


3. **The Certified Refurbisher / Technician:**
* *Goal:* List batch-inspected, component-repaired units with certified tier labels.
* *Requirement:* Bulk diagnostic entry, serialized quality certification, trusted seller badges.


4. **Platform Administrator & Dispute Auditor:**
* *Goal:* Prevent fraudulent IMEI listings, resolve peer-to-peer disputes, maintain catalog integrity.



### 2.2 End-to-End User Journey Walkthroughs

| Stage | Buyer Path | Seller Path | Refurbisher Path |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Discovery** | Parametric search & faceted hardware filtering | Navigates to dynamic valuation engine | Connects bulk inventory via API/Portal |
| **Verification** | Inspects 32-point diagnostic matrix & battery % | Inputs serial/IMEI & cosmetic parameters | Uploads hardware test lab report |
| **Negotiation** | Dispatches structured bid via offer drawer | Accepts, rejects, or counters offer | Fixed price with warranty guarantee |
| **Fulfillment** | Secure escrow checkout / local rendezvous code | Receives packing slip / rendezvous token | Automated logistics pickup |
| **Settlement** | Diagnostic verification window (48 hours) | Funds released from escrow | Bi-weekly consolidated payout |

