## Module 3: Functional & Non-Functional Requirements (SRS)

### 3.1 Functional Requirements (FR)

* **FR-01 (Device Cataloging):** The system shall categorize listings by Brand, Model Family, Variant, Internal Storage, RAM, and Baseband Carrier Status.
* **FR-02 (Inspection Scorecard):** Every listing must render an immutable diagnostic record covering display integrity, biometric sensors, camera optics, chassis condition, and battery health capacity percentage.
* **FR-03 (Automated Valuation Engine):** The platform must compute a real-time recommended market price using a deterministic pricing algorithm that decrements MSRP based on age, storage, wear grade, and battery decay.
* **FR-04 (Bilateral Negotiation):** The system must facilitate non-binding or escrow-backed counter-offers restricted to ±25% of the asking price to prevent extreme spam bids.
* **FR-05 (Real-Time Communication):** The platform must provide an encapsulated peer-to-peer messaging sandbox with automated initial seller response fallbacks.

### 3.2 Non-Functional Requirements (NFR)

* **NFR-01 (Performance & Latency):** Client-side catalog filtering across a dataset of up to 5,000 active memory nodes must evaluate in less than 16 milliseconds (maintaining 60 FPS UI rendering).
* **NFR-02 (Zero-External Asset Resilience):** The core presentation interface must compile within single-page self-contained modules without relying on unversioned third-party styling assets.
* **NFR-03 (Security & Sanitization):** All chat messages, listing inputs, and pricing fields must be strictly sanitized against Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) and DOM injection vulnerabilities.
* **NFR-04 (Availability & Offline Tolerance):** The client state (wishlists, draft listings, active conversation threads) must persist through client storage (Web Storage API / IndexedDB) across sessions.

