## Module 6: Algorithmic Pricing & Depreciation Mathematics

The RePhone valuation engine calculates fair market price using multi-variable decay formulas rather than arbitrary subjective inputs.

### 6.1 Base Depreciation Formula

The fair market value $P_{\text{fair}}$ of any smartphone is modeled as:

$$P_{\text{fair}} = P_{\text{MSRP}} \times D_{\text{age}}(t) \times C_{\text{grade}} \times B_{\text{health}} \times S_{\text{factor}}$$

Where:

* $P_{\text{MSRP}}$: Initial retail launch price of the specific model and storage tier.
* $D_{\text{age}}(t)$: Non-linear temporal depreciation coefficient as a function of age in years $t$:

$$D_{\text{age}}(t) = e^{-\lambda t}$$



*(Where $\lambda \approx 0.28$ for flagship iOS devices and $\lambda \approx 0.38$ for Android devices due to historical secondary market retention rates).*
* $C_{\text{grade}}$: Cosmetic condition multiplier:
* Like New ($A^+$): $1.00$
* Excellent ($A$): $0.90$
* Good ($B$): $0.78$
* Fair ($C$): $0.62$


* $B_{\text{health}}$: Battery degradation impact factor (where $H$ is the current health capacity percentage $[50 \dots 100]$):

$$B_{\text{health}} = \begin{cases} 1.00 & \text{if } H \ge 90 \\ 1.00 - (0.008 \times (90 - H)) & \text{if } 80 \le H < 90 \\ 0.92 - (0.015 \times (80 - H)) & \text{if } H < 80 \end{cases}$$


* $S_{\text{factor}}$: Storage capacity scalar ($1.00$ for base storage, $+0.08$ for 256GB, $+0.16$ for 512GB, $+0.24$ for 1TB).

