## Module 9: Frontend Architecture & Component Implementation

The single-page client implementation relies on modular JavaScript functions adhering to Model-View-Controller (MVC) principles:

### 9.1 Core State Objects

* `state.catalog`: Master array containing all device nodes (initial mock database combined with user submissions).
* `state.filters`: Active query state (`brand`, `condition`, `storage`, `maxPrice`, `searchQuery`, `certifiedOnly`).
* `state.wishlist`: Set of active listing IDs mapped to browser storage.
* `state.activeChat`: Thread metadata and communication history between active buyer and target seller.

### 9.2 Rendering Cycle

```
[Event Trigger] ──► [Mutate state.filters] ──► [Execute filterEngine()] ──► [Virtual DOM Diff/HTML Build] ──► [Paint DOM]

```

